1
00:00:04,105 --> 00:00:06,596
Ladies and gentlemen...

2
00:00:06,733 --> 00:00:10,944
it's a pleasure for me to be here
on such a beautiful day...

3
00:00:11,154 --> 00:00:13,905
in the great city of Detroit.

4
00:00:15,116 --> 00:00:17,785
And I'd love to tell you all...

5
00:00:17,994 --> 00:00:21,493
to sit back, relax
and enjoy yourselves.

6
00:00:22,081 --> 00:00:23,955
I'd love to...

7
00:00:24,125 --> 00:00:27,245
but unfortunately,
I can't do that.

8
00:00:27,754 --> 00:00:32,297
There's a very serious issue spiraling
out of control in this country.

9
00:00:32,467 --> 00:00:35,883
Illegal handguns ending up
in the hands of our children.

10
00:00:39,182 --> 00:00:43,974
Instead of reading off statistics
that you might not already know...

11
00:00:44,187 --> 00:00:49,264
that last year, more preschoolers died
from guns than police officers...

12
00:00:49,484 --> 00:00:52,983
or that gunshot wounds are the
second leading cause of death...

13
00:00:53,154 --> 00:00:55,562
for all people in the
U.S., ages 10 to 34.

14
00:00:58,451 --> 00:01:01,024
Hold it. Go on in.

15
00:01:21,683 --> 00:01:25,301
While he lay
bleeding to death for 40 minutes...

16
00:01:25,395 --> 00:01:28,064
waiting for help to come.

17
00:01:28,147 --> 00:01:30,555
Darren was 16 years old.

18
00:01:31,025 --> 00:01:33,979
That could've been any one
of your children.

19
00:01:34,946 --> 00:01:38,896
I hope you'll consider my four-year
plan to get guns off the streets.

20
00:01:39,993 --> 00:01:42,069
I need your help and your support.

21
00:01:42,745 --> 00:01:46,957
Let's stop the pain and suffering
Darren's family had to go through.

22
00:01:47,041 --> 00:01:48,868
God bless you and thank you.

23
00:01:52,088 --> 00:01:56,002
- He just loves pissing me off.
- I'm sure he has his reasons.

24
00:02:04,058 --> 00:02:05,517
Thanks a lot.

25
00:02:07,228 --> 00:02:08,557
Thank you.

26
00:02:13,902 --> 00:02:14,850
Relax.

27
00:02:15,194 --> 00:02:16,439
I'll talk to him.

28
00:02:16,696 --> 00:02:18,238
Thank you, everybody.

29
00:02:18,448 --> 00:02:21,069
How are you? Good to see you.

30
00:02:22,035 --> 00:02:23,826
Mr. Vice President, sir?

31
00:03:08,957 --> 00:03:10,949
Bobby, what the hell is this?

32
00:03:11,834 --> 00:03:13,210
You believe this guy?

33
00:03:29,435 --> 00:03:32,602
Sorry, the bridge is closed
until the V.P. gets across.

34
00:03:32,814 --> 00:03:35,186
You can't stay here.
You have to move it out.

35
00:03:46,578 --> 00:03:48,784
- Shit!
- Get down, sir!

36
00:03:48,871 --> 00:03:50,414
Get us out of here!

37
00:03:57,297 --> 00:03:58,328
Excuse me.

38
00:04:00,717 --> 00:04:03,468
Officers need help!
On the bridge! Shots fired!

39
00:04:03,636 --> 00:04:06,258
Warn the D.P., they
are dressed as cops!

40
00:04:06,347 --> 00:04:08,174
Repeat: They are dressed as cops!

41
00:04:08,600 --> 00:04:11,007
Alpha six to Bravo
Air, keep cover...

42
00:04:15,982 --> 00:04:18,687
- Stay down!
- What is going on?

43
00:04:20,236 --> 00:04:22,988
No cops on the bridge.
We can't tell who's who.

44
00:04:23,197 --> 00:04:26,115
No Detroit P.D.,
Secret Service only.

45
00:04:28,202 --> 00:04:30,575
Officers need help.
Motorcade's under attack!

46
00:04:30,663 --> 00:04:34,115
All units, stay off the
bridge, as per Secret Service.

47
00:04:43,051 --> 00:04:45,090
All units stay off bridge...

48
00:04:45,178 --> 00:04:47,420
Goddamn it, I told you
to clear the bridge!

49
00:04:47,680 --> 00:04:49,388
Bring the truck in!

50
00:04:54,270 --> 00:04:56,559
Goddamn it!
Secret Service only!

51
00:04:56,773 --> 00:04:58,101
Who the hell is that?

52
00:05:11,704 --> 00:05:12,700
Get me out!

53
00:05:18,962 --> 00:05:20,539
- Get me out of here!
- Get in.

54
00:05:20,755 --> 00:05:22,831
Who the hell are you?
Off the bridge.

55
00:05:22,924 --> 00:05:25,296
We're not moving till
the transport arrives.

56
00:05:25,385 --> 00:05:28,136
I'm not talking to you!
Mr. Vice President, get in here!

57
00:05:30,807 --> 00:05:32,680
We need help here now!

58
00:05:34,435 --> 00:05:36,511
Alpha one to Alpha six.

59
00:05:39,065 --> 00:05:41,603
Move it out! Everything's
under control!

60
00:05:42,443 --> 00:05:43,190
Jesus!

61
00:05:43,278 --> 00:05:45,401
Take out the Alpha vehicle!

62
00:06:37,957 --> 00:06:40,164
I'm sorry, sir. I got to do this.

63
00:06:40,335 --> 00:06:43,336
Shit! I can't swim.

64
00:06:54,515 --> 00:06:55,891
Don't move!

65
00:07:02,357 --> 00:07:03,519
Freeze!

66
00:07:03,733 --> 00:07:06,022
It's okay. I'm on the job.

67
00:07:11,991 --> 00:07:13,485
We got you, sir.

68
00:07:13,576 --> 00:07:15,450
You're going to be all right, sir.

69
00:07:20,124 --> 00:07:23,624
Why did you drive onto that
bridge and start World War III?

70
00:07:23,836 --> 00:07:26,506
- I saved his life, Frank.
- You were lucky, Orin.

71
00:07:26,589 --> 00:07:27,752
Extremely lucky.

72
00:07:27,840 --> 00:07:31,256
The Secret Service gave a direct
order not to storm that bridge!

73
00:07:31,511 --> 00:07:34,084
They were responsible for him.
Not you!

74
00:07:34,472 --> 00:07:37,259
- What if it went the other way?
- I didn't vote for him.

75
00:07:37,350 --> 00:07:38,844
This is funny to you?

76
00:07:39,060 --> 00:07:41,017
- What's funny to me is...
- Cut it out.

77
00:07:42,939 --> 00:07:44,018
Who were they?

78
00:07:44,691 --> 00:07:46,399
Some Michigan militant group.

79
00:07:46,901 --> 00:07:48,810
- Live by the sword, man.
- Sit down.

80
00:07:55,702 --> 00:07:58,453
Look, Orin. We've known
each other a long time.

81
00:07:59,205 --> 00:08:01,198
I am your friend,
but also your boss.

82
00:08:01,416 --> 00:08:05,034
As your friend, you don't follow orders.
You're unmanageable.

83
00:08:05,253 --> 00:08:07,744
You don't obey the law
or think before you act.

84
00:08:07,964 --> 00:08:11,131
And now, as your
boss, you're fired.

85
00:08:11,384 --> 00:08:13,507
- Just like that.
- Hinges wants you out.

86
00:08:13,720 --> 00:08:15,214
There's nothing I can do.

87
00:08:15,471 --> 00:08:17,879
You want to talk to him yourself,
be my guest.

88
00:08:17,974 --> 00:08:19,385
Now handle it!

89
00:08:26,816 --> 00:08:29,224
You are like a cockroach, Mr. Boyd.

90
00:08:29,402 --> 00:08:32,853
Every time I try to get rid of you,
you appeal to the union...

91
00:08:32,947 --> 00:08:35,403
and they send your
ass right back here.

92
00:08:35,909 --> 00:08:37,107
But not this time.

93
00:08:37,827 --> 00:08:41,659
I've been talking to the Secret Service
figuring out what to do with you.

94
00:08:42,332 --> 00:08:44,158
They want you to suffer, Mr. Boyd.

95
00:08:44,584 --> 00:08:47,751
They want you to suffer bad
for that stupid stunt you pulled.

96
00:08:48,504 --> 00:08:51,838
And I must say, I do not disagree.

97
00:08:52,425 --> 00:08:54,216
You guys are unbelievable.

98
00:08:54,427 --> 00:08:57,000
I saw a problem, I fixed it.
Simple as that.

99
00:08:57,263 --> 00:08:59,137
That's bullshit, Mr. Boyd.

100
00:08:59,349 --> 00:09:01,425
Because of cops like you...

101
00:09:02,101 --> 00:09:04,177
police have a bad image everywhere.

102
00:09:04,604 --> 00:09:07,724
You won't pin that on me.
I stick my neck out every day.

103
00:09:07,941 --> 00:09:11,606
You remind me of bureaucrats in the
'60s sending kids to fight in Vietnam.

104
00:09:11,778 --> 00:09:13,901
I'm not going to
send you to Vietnam.

105
00:09:13,988 --> 00:09:16,942
- I'm going to send you to the 15th.
- That shithole.

106
00:09:17,033 --> 00:09:18,693
You'll fit right in.

107
00:09:35,051 --> 00:09:36,545
Come on, get up.

108
00:09:37,387 --> 00:09:39,260
I know my rights, man.

109
00:09:40,932 --> 00:09:42,343
Knock off the shit!

110
00:09:42,934 --> 00:09:44,096
Understand?

111
00:09:45,353 --> 00:09:46,847
Can I help you?

112
00:09:47,063 --> 00:09:49,388
I'm looking for the
ringleader of this circus.

113
00:09:49,899 --> 00:09:52,058
Yes, sir. And you are?

114
00:09:52,151 --> 00:09:55,485
- Boyd. The commander's expecting me.
- Follow me.

115
00:09:56,573 --> 00:09:58,530
Commander's got a grip on things.

116
00:09:58,741 --> 00:10:01,067
I've seen mental wards
saner than this place.

117
00:10:25,435 --> 00:10:26,633
Can we start over?

118
00:10:27,186 --> 00:10:30,022
Too late for first
impressions. Sit.

119
00:10:36,529 --> 00:10:38,321
This year alone...

120
00:10:38,406 --> 00:10:41,490
three complaints filed against
you for excessive force.

121
00:10:41,576 --> 00:10:43,865
This doesn't seem like
a hero's welcome.

122
00:10:43,953 --> 00:10:46,658
You want to be welcomed?
Stay out of the headlines.

123
00:10:46,748 --> 00:10:49,239
Around here,
there's no such thing as heroes.

124
00:10:49,334 --> 00:10:53,118
I've got community activists swearing
we treat everybody like criminals...

125
00:10:53,212 --> 00:10:55,750
and criminals all swearing
they're altar boys.

126
00:10:55,840 --> 00:10:58,924
Maybe I was never an altar boy,
but the point is...

127
00:10:59,177 --> 00:11:02,546
The point is, cops don't
uphold the law by breaking it.

128
00:11:03,681 --> 00:11:06,468
Now, you got a problem in
my house, you come see me.

129
00:11:06,643 --> 00:11:09,597
None of this Lone Ranger stuff
that I keep hearing about.

130
00:11:10,563 --> 00:11:12,022
Are you listening?

131
00:11:12,106 --> 00:11:14,858
If I have a problem,
I'll come and see the commander.

132
00:11:14,943 --> 00:11:18,608
All that stuff with the Vice President?
A little water never hurt anybody.

133
00:11:18,696 --> 00:11:22,315
But I am worried
about your discipline problem.

134
00:11:22,659 --> 00:11:24,984
I was thinking about
putting you on a desk.

135
00:11:25,370 --> 00:11:27,943
- I can't type.
- I have a better idea.

136
00:11:28,915 --> 00:11:32,366
Something that will
broaden your horizons.

137
00:11:34,462 --> 00:11:35,743
And then her dog.

138
00:11:37,715 --> 00:11:40,289
Her dog gets so freaked out...

139
00:11:40,718 --> 00:11:44,170
he takes this enormous shit...

140
00:11:44,389 --> 00:11:46,796
right in the middle
of the living room.

141
00:11:50,144 --> 00:11:52,635
I chased that little
bastard everywhere...

142
00:11:53,147 --> 00:11:54,974
until I finally cornered him.

143
00:11:55,066 --> 00:11:57,604
I warned her not to buy
a frigging poodle.

144
00:11:57,819 --> 00:12:00,985
I never could have thrown
a German Shepherd out the window.

145
00:12:05,285 --> 00:12:06,483
Okay.

146
00:12:14,794 --> 00:12:16,419
That's it. Let it out.

147
00:12:16,504 --> 00:12:19,078
Okay? That's why we're here.

148
00:12:19,299 --> 00:12:22,999
To talk through our problems,
not to let it bottle up.

149
00:12:23,219 --> 00:12:24,250
Okay.

150
00:12:24,846 --> 00:12:28,012
And the rest of you,
I want you to dig down deep...

151
00:12:28,266 --> 00:12:30,638
and ask yourself the question:

152
00:12:31,519 --> 00:12:35,054
Why are we mad and
what are we mad at?

153
00:12:36,566 --> 00:12:38,025
Good. Okay.

154
00:12:39,694 --> 00:12:41,437
Who'd like to go next?

155
00:12:43,031 --> 00:12:44,193
Hey, everyone.

156
00:12:44,282 --> 00:12:45,231
How are you?

157
00:12:45,325 --> 00:12:49,322
For those of you just tuning in, my name
is Henry Wayne, and I'm a rageaholic.

158
00:12:49,412 --> 00:12:52,496
You probably all recognize me
from my show, Detroit A.M.

159
00:12:54,667 --> 00:12:57,621
You're probably wondering
what happened to my head here.

160
00:12:57,712 --> 00:13:00,915
I know it's always something,
and I shouldn't lose my cool.

161
00:13:01,007 --> 00:13:03,463
I was at Krispy Kreme,
picking up a twelve-pack.

162
00:13:03,551 --> 00:13:05,093
- And this guy...
- Okay.

163
00:13:05,303 --> 00:13:08,008
I'm so sorry to
interrupt you but...

164
00:13:08,973 --> 00:13:11,215
I'm kind of looking
for a fresh face next.

165
00:13:11,309 --> 00:13:12,472
I've been sitting there....

166
00:13:12,560 --> 00:13:13,971
We'll get back to you.

167
00:13:14,062 --> 00:13:16,979
I'm a ticking time bomb,
and I'm ready to implode.

168
00:13:17,065 --> 00:13:18,559
Let's solve my problem.

169
00:13:18,983 --> 00:13:19,932
Sit down!

170
00:13:24,530 --> 00:13:25,526
Okay.

171
00:13:26,532 --> 00:13:28,609
So, who's it going to be?

172
00:13:31,579 --> 00:13:35,328
Mr. Boyd? I believe that
you were sent to us...

173
00:13:35,416 --> 00:13:37,872
because of work-related stress...

174
00:13:38,086 --> 00:13:40,328
aggression towards
authority figures...

175
00:13:40,588 --> 00:13:43,589
and an all-around
lack of discipline.

176
00:13:43,758 --> 00:13:47,756
I'm fine. You can move on.
Other people want to say something.

177
00:13:47,929 --> 00:13:52,555
Mr. Boyd, denial is a classic
symptom of unhealthy rage.

178
00:13:52,767 --> 00:13:55,803
Okay? So why don't
you just stand up...

179
00:13:56,020 --> 00:13:58,891
and tell us a little
bit about yourself.

180
00:14:16,708 --> 00:14:19,709
I don't have rage.

181
00:14:19,794 --> 00:14:21,870
I'm a happy guy. You see this face?

182
00:14:22,797 --> 00:14:24,955
This is a happy face. You all...

183
00:14:25,300 --> 00:14:28,135
would be lucky to be
as happy as I am.

184
00:14:48,948 --> 00:14:50,988
What am I, a shit magnet?

185
00:14:56,164 --> 00:14:57,991
Junior, having a tough time?

186
00:14:58,082 --> 00:15:01,083
You got to get in and out quick.
I'm an expert at this.

187
00:15:01,169 --> 00:15:03,078
I could do that in
a blink of an eye.

188
00:15:03,171 --> 00:15:05,709
- Why don't you show us?
- Watch.

189
00:15:06,799 --> 00:15:09,337
- Just like that. See?
- You a magician?

190
00:15:09,469 --> 00:15:12,672
You want me to show you how to
pull a rabbit out of your ass?

191
00:15:13,973 --> 00:15:16,381
Screw Linda. Come on back in.

192
00:15:16,476 --> 00:15:18,883
Everybody's tearing
the tops off their desks.

193
00:15:19,103 --> 00:15:20,598
Who the hell are you?

194
00:15:20,688 --> 00:15:22,728
Henry Wayne. Detroit A.M.

195
00:15:23,358 --> 00:15:25,350
- This a friend of yours?
- Yeah.

196
00:15:25,568 --> 00:15:28,273
- Go back to class.
- They're gonna kill me without you.

197
00:15:28,363 --> 00:15:31,529
If you stay here, they might kill
you, too, so go back to class.

198
00:15:34,244 --> 00:15:36,153
Jeez! Well, no! Well, shit!

199
00:15:36,371 --> 00:15:38,162
I don't even know this guy.

200
00:15:38,665 --> 00:15:42,365
Stay out of our class. We got
people in there with real problems.

201
00:15:42,794 --> 00:15:46,127
FYI, next week
I'm doing a show on violent twins.

202
00:15:46,214 --> 00:15:48,456
- Enough of this bullshit!
- You're not twins?

203
00:15:48,675 --> 00:15:49,955
Take the man's keys.

204
00:15:50,051 --> 00:15:51,331
Give me your keys.

205
00:16:22,792 --> 00:16:25,579
Stop it!
Mr. Boyd, stop hitting that man!

206
00:16:28,965 --> 00:16:32,713
Mr. Boyd! What're you doing? This
is no way to deal with your anger.

207
00:16:32,802 --> 00:16:35,969
Screw that, man! You kill those
bastards! They tried to pop us!

208
00:16:37,515 --> 00:16:40,053
Did you guys see that?
Can you believe this shit?

209
00:16:40,226 --> 00:16:44,058
Boyd is such a bad-ass. He could easily
win a tough-men competition.

210
00:16:44,147 --> 00:16:47,350
You guys just missed it,
but I'm glad I got here when I did.

211
00:16:47,567 --> 00:16:51,018
Boyd's a cop! He's a cop!
He gets to do this shit all the time!

212
00:16:51,237 --> 00:16:53,562
We're going to have
great stories for group!

213
00:16:56,993 --> 00:16:58,902
You see how happy I make others?

214
00:17:03,207 --> 00:17:04,406
Hey, Boyd.

215
00:17:06,336 --> 00:17:07,913
Good job, man.

216
00:17:11,049 --> 00:17:12,459
We'll see you next week?

217
00:17:15,261 --> 00:17:17,301
Come on, guys! That was great!

218
00:17:17,513 --> 00:17:19,720
Now, was that cool, or what?
Come on!

219
00:17:54,092 --> 00:17:55,835
Who are you here to see?

220
00:17:56,052 --> 00:17:57,167
Shaun Rollins.

221
00:17:57,637 --> 00:17:59,511
- And you are?
- A friend.

222
00:18:00,223 --> 00:18:01,800
Photo I.D.

223
00:18:05,687 --> 00:18:06,967
Sign in.

224
00:18:10,608 --> 00:18:12,186
Back to the left.

225
00:18:30,837 --> 00:18:32,461
How you holding up?

226
00:18:33,423 --> 00:18:34,668
Not too well, man.

227
00:18:35,216 --> 00:18:37,209
Straight losing it, dog.

228
00:18:37,385 --> 00:18:39,710
I can only take so
much of this shit.

229
00:18:39,887 --> 00:18:43,221
- What's up with my lawyer?
- I talked to him.

230
00:18:43,433 --> 00:18:45,639
Slow motion. You know, the system.

231
00:18:45,852 --> 00:18:47,726
No, I don't know, man.

232
00:18:48,104 --> 00:18:50,429
I need to know
how much time I'm looking at.

233
00:18:50,523 --> 00:18:52,516
Nobody's telling me nothing.

234
00:18:55,111 --> 00:18:56,356
I don't know.

235
00:18:59,198 --> 00:19:00,574
Fuck, man.

236
00:19:01,117 --> 00:19:02,860
This shit is bullshit.

237
00:19:03,536 --> 00:19:05,743
Fuck do you mean, you don't know?

238
00:19:06,539 --> 00:19:09,540
You got to see the Jeffrey Dahmer
look-alikes in here, man.

239
00:19:09,626 --> 00:19:11,250
It's crazy.

240
00:19:11,920 --> 00:19:15,371
It's like I can't even turn my back
to take a piss up in here, man.

241
00:19:18,801 --> 00:19:19,797
Shaun.

242
00:19:20,011 --> 00:19:21,042
Shaun.

243
00:19:25,975 --> 00:19:27,968
You got to stay focused.

244
00:19:29,812 --> 00:19:33,016
Do whatever you got to do to make
sure that you safe in there.

245
00:19:35,318 --> 00:19:37,357
I got everything on
the street covered.

246
00:19:38,446 --> 00:19:40,154
Nobody's forgotten about you.

247
00:19:43,618 --> 00:19:44,946
Nobody.

248
00:20:16,776 --> 00:20:18,685
