00:56:14,764 --> 00:56:18,264
This is to us finally getting
together for dinner.

744
00:56:19,644 --> 00:56:21,352
But I just have one request.

745
00:56:22,105 --> 00:56:23,433
I'm listening.

746
00:56:23,648 --> 00:56:24,811
No police talk.

747
00:56:25,316 --> 00:56:28,317
No mentioning the latest homicide
or gang shooting.

748
00:56:29,154 --> 00:56:31,526
Tonight, just happy
thoughts. Agreed?

749
00:56:31,740 --> 00:56:34,147
Agreed. To happy thoughts.

750
00:56:36,494 --> 00:56:38,154
Good evening, Commander.

751
00:56:40,415 --> 00:56:42,075
What're you doing here, Boyd?

752
00:56:42,167 --> 00:56:44,918
- You wanted to see me.
- In my office, not here.

753
00:56:45,003 --> 00:56:46,912
But I'm here now. So let's talk.

754
00:56:47,005 --> 00:56:49,840
I'm sorry, but we were
actually right in the middle.

755
00:56:50,550 --> 00:56:52,009
Why don't you take a walk?

756
00:56:53,261 --> 00:56:56,179
It's okay. Just give
us five minutes.

757
00:56:58,933 --> 00:57:01,140
I had to go
to the men's room anyway.

758
00:57:05,482 --> 00:57:08,436
- How'd you find me?
- What are you doing with this guy?

759
00:57:08,526 --> 00:57:10,899
That is none of your business.

760
00:57:11,112 --> 00:57:14,481
- He doesn't look right for you.
- And you do?

761
00:57:15,658 --> 00:57:17,817
What did you want to
talk to me about?

762
00:57:17,911 --> 00:57:19,654
Why'd you visit Shaun Rollins?

763
00:57:19,746 --> 00:57:23,115
- The walls have ears.
- I know everything, Boyd.

764
00:57:23,500 --> 00:57:25,160
So, why am I here?

765
00:57:25,377 --> 00:57:27,868
I don't have time for games.
What are you up to?

766
00:57:28,880 --> 00:57:31,715
- You used to work for Internal Affairs.
- Yeah.

767
00:57:31,841 --> 00:57:35,921
Out of all the people around you,
how'd you know who you could trust?

768
00:57:36,554 --> 00:57:38,097
Why? What have you got?

769
00:57:38,181 --> 00:57:42,013
I can't say yet. Not till I have
more proof. What have you got?

770
00:57:42,477 --> 00:57:45,893
Let's just say my instincts tell me
something's not quite right.

771
00:57:47,649 --> 00:57:49,143
Bring me something solid.

772
00:57:49,234 --> 00:57:50,728
I have something solid.

773
00:57:51,194 --> 00:57:52,225
More solid.

774
00:57:52,946 --> 00:57:56,481
- Then I'll know what to do with it.
- You'll know what to do with it?

775
00:57:58,118 --> 00:57:59,446
- Carmine?
- Good.

776
00:58:01,162 --> 00:58:03,570
Not bad. I'll see you on campus.

777
00:58:11,256 --> 00:58:12,631
Orin?

778
00:58:13,967 --> 00:58:15,046
Watch your back.

779
00:58:39,909 --> 00:58:41,736
Hey, Clark. What's going on?

780
00:58:41,953 --> 00:58:43,993
Six. Nothing much.

781
00:58:44,205 --> 00:58:47,123
I hear you're working
with Supercop now.

782
00:58:47,500 --> 00:58:48,781
What's that like?

783
00:58:48,877 --> 00:58:51,368
Hey, George. Which one are you?
Starsky or Hutch?

784
00:58:52,672 --> 00:58:53,787
Don't mind him.

785
00:58:54,174 --> 00:58:55,336
I don't.

786
00:58:58,136 --> 00:59:00,425
Heard about that scuffle.

787
00:59:00,597 --> 00:59:02,922
What were you doing
at The Static anyway?

788
00:59:03,224 --> 00:59:05,264
Orin wanted to question
the owner, T.K.

789
00:59:05,852 --> 00:59:06,848
About what?

790
00:59:07,687 --> 00:59:08,968
They never spoke.

791
00:59:09,189 --> 00:59:11,395
Boyd's trying to steal
my bust, George.

792
00:59:11,608 --> 00:59:14,146
He's a glory hound.
We've seen this kind before.

793
00:59:14,402 --> 00:59:16,146
What else did you find out?

794
00:59:16,237 --> 00:59:18,693
Nothing. We searched his office,
came up empty.

795
00:59:18,782 --> 00:59:21,320
I wish you would have called
the point detective.

796
00:59:21,409 --> 00:59:22,987
I would've found something.

797
00:59:23,078 --> 00:59:26,992
We did find a visitor's pass from
County. Don't worry, Montini.

798
00:59:27,082 --> 00:59:29,205
We'll let you know
what we come up with.

799
00:59:34,130 --> 00:59:35,838
You guys done with the bench?

800
00:59:36,257 --> 00:59:37,835
Yeah, go ahead.

801
00:59:37,926 --> 00:59:39,420
Hey, you know, Montini?

802
00:59:39,511 --> 00:59:42,547
If all you come down here
to do is work out your mouth...

803
00:59:42,764 --> 00:59:45,516
maybe you should move on.
Breaks our concentration.

804
00:59:54,484 --> 00:59:56,642
Find out who they
visited up at County.

805
00:59:56,736 --> 00:59:58,978
Yeah, don't worry about
that, I'm on it.

806
01:00:28,309 --> 01:00:29,638
You come with me.

807
01:00:29,811 --> 01:00:31,436
Be back in an hour.

808
01:00:44,951 --> 01:00:46,576
Ready to meet the wizard?

809
01:00:48,872 --> 01:00:50,247
Put it on.

810
01:00:54,169 --> 01:00:56,410
You don't need to know
where we're going.

811
01:00:58,006 --> 01:01:00,876
Welcome to the inner sanctum,
Mr. Walker.

812
01:01:04,512 --> 01:01:05,923
I always wanted to do that.

813
01:01:06,222 --> 01:01:07,503
I wish I had a cat.

814
01:01:07,766 --> 01:01:09,141
Heard a lot about you.

815
01:01:09,225 --> 01:01:10,803
Wish I could say the same.

816
01:01:11,603 --> 01:01:13,679
Like the saying goes:

817
01:01:14,022 --> 01:01:18,435
"The greatest trick the devil ever pulled
was convince the world he didn't exist."

818
01:01:19,486 --> 01:01:21,110
Let me show you around.

819
01:01:46,679 --> 01:01:48,672
I don't get it. T-shirts?

820
01:01:48,765 --> 01:01:51,635
Amazing what you can do
with the right chemicals.

821
01:01:51,726 --> 01:01:54,976
Your connections are all over the
country, this is our plan...

822
01:01:55,063 --> 01:01:56,972
to get the heroin out of state.

823
01:01:57,065 --> 01:01:59,817
No risky exposure,
no trail back to us.

824
01:01:59,901 --> 01:02:03,270
These T-shirts are dipped
in a heroin solution...

825
01:02:04,072 --> 01:02:06,397
and dried under these lamps.

826
01:02:06,866 --> 01:02:09,274
They're folded and
sealed in shrink-wrap.

827
01:02:10,578 --> 01:02:12,238
Dogs can't even smell it.

828
01:02:12,414 --> 01:02:14,323
You can send them
anywhere you want.

829
01:02:14,416 --> 01:02:15,910
Extract the heroin later.

830
01:02:16,751 --> 01:02:17,866
You in?

831
01:02:21,089 --> 01:02:22,085
Yeah, I'm in.

832
01:02:24,050 --> 01:02:25,628
Pick you up at midnight.

833
01:02:44,320 --> 01:02:47,855
Me and the I Team came up
with some fascinating intel.

834
01:02:48,033 --> 01:02:50,488
Latrell Walker's whole I.D.'s fake.
He's a shell.

835
01:02:50,577 --> 01:02:52,783
He paid a lot too.
He's got everything.

836
01:02:52,871 --> 01:02:55,492
Driver's license, birth certificate,
credit cards.

837
01:02:55,582 --> 01:02:57,870
He's even got a voter's
registration card.

838
01:02:57,959 --> 01:03:00,628
Normal investigation
wouldn't have uncovered this...

839
01:03:00,712 --> 01:03:05,006
but one of our dudes worked for the
IrS, and can computer-dissect anybody.

840
01:03:05,091 --> 01:03:06,502
Who is he, then?

841
01:03:06,718 --> 01:03:08,461
He's Shaun Rollins' brother.

842
01:03:08,803 --> 01:03:09,835
Listen to this.

843
01:03:09,929 --> 01:03:13,713
About six months ago, Latrell's
little brother, Shaun, gets popped.

844
01:03:13,892 --> 01:03:17,676
He claims the heroin was planted, but
the cops made the charges stick.

845
01:03:17,771 --> 01:03:20,309
Next thing you know,
Latrell's back in town.

846
01:03:20,398 --> 01:03:22,355
That's why he was visiting him.

847
01:03:22,442 --> 01:03:26,653
My sources ran a check on Shaun
also, and he's set for life financially.

848
01:03:26,738 --> 01:03:28,113
How? From who?

849
01:03:28,406 --> 01:03:31,360
He has a trust fund
set up in his name for millions...

850
01:03:31,451 --> 01:03:33,408
but he can't touch
it until he's 25.

851
01:03:33,495 --> 01:03:36,282
- Who set it up for him?
- I'm getting to that.

852
01:03:36,373 --> 01:03:39,742
Shaun also has another brother,
Leon. Or so I thought.

853
01:03:39,834 --> 01:03:43,369
Now, Leon Rollins and Latrell
Walker are the same person.

854
01:03:43,463 --> 01:03:44,922
You're shitting me.

855
01:03:45,006 --> 01:03:47,331
Leon's also a gazillionaire.

856
01:03:47,717 --> 01:03:51,217
How can a guy with no record
make so much money dealing heroin?

857
01:03:51,304 --> 01:03:53,795
No, no. The guy's a computer wiz.

858
01:03:54,015 --> 01:03:57,680
Started up a dot com out of Virginia
called $9.99 Dot Com.

859
01:03:57,769 --> 01:03:59,596
"Anything you want under $10."

860
01:03:59,688 --> 01:04:04,100
And he did great. Lucky bastard cashed
out just before the bubble burst.

861
01:04:04,192 --> 01:04:08,901
Maybe Latrell's buying heroin, and
seeking distributors on the Internet.

862
01:04:09,030 --> 01:04:11,070
Welcome to the Computer
Age, my friend.

863
01:04:11,282 --> 01:04:14,402
No street involvement,
no watching out for cops, no risk.

864
01:04:14,494 --> 01:04:16,534
It's brilliant, isn't it?

865
01:04:17,497 --> 01:04:20,414
It still doesn't add up
unless they have some big debts.

866
01:04:20,500 --> 01:04:24,118
Well, here's all the paperwork.
I got IPO statements, tax returns.

867
01:04:24,212 --> 01:04:27,248
I got his address from a crooked
car dealer we investigated.

868
01:04:27,340 --> 01:04:29,914
I don't know if it will
help, but I did my job.

869
01:04:30,677 --> 01:04:31,957
You did good, man.

870
01:04:33,221 --> 01:04:34,051
Thanks, partner.

871
01:06:05,605 --> 01:06:07,064
Let's go. Smash it!

872
01:06:10,902 --> 01:06:12,313
Let's move it!

873
01:06:31,339 --> 01:06:33,830
Montini, Useldinger...

874
01:06:34,008 --> 01:06:35,503
what a surprise.

875
01:06:37,137 --> 01:06:38,595
This to make me talk?

876
01:06:38,680 --> 01:06:40,423
No, it's to make you die.

877
01:06:40,515 --> 01:06:43,599
It's from Latrell. He made us
an offer we couldn't refuse.

878
01:06:59,159 --> 01:07:00,439
Look out!

879
01:07:04,622 --> 01:07:06,165
Shoot him!

880
01:08:45,640 --> 01:08:48,214
You don't have the balls
to kill me yourself.

881
01:08:48,309 --> 01:08:50,635
You don't know what
you're talking about.

882
01:08:52,939 --> 01:08:55,228
- I know everything about you.
- About time.

883
01:08:55,316 --> 01:08:57,060
But why would I want you dead?

884
01:08:57,152 --> 01:09:00,188
Because I'm that close to locking
you up with your brother.

885
01:09:22,761 --> 01:09:25,880
You want to see
what's really going on?

886
01:09:29,851 --> 01:09:31,014
Come on.

887
01:09:46,201 --> 01:09:48,822
It's all right,
it's all right. Chill.

888
01:09:50,038 --> 01:09:51,449
This is my operation.

889
01:09:54,501 --> 01:09:57,418
- What's up, man?
- Yeah, it's all right.

890
01:10:01,216 --> 01:10:03,292
I believe you two have already met.

891
01:10:04,928 --> 01:10:06,801
What the hell're you doing here?

892
01:10:06,888 --> 01:10:08,715
You want another ass-whupping?

893
01:10:09,140 --> 01:10:11,596
I'm joking. I got your
grill downstairs.

894
01:10:11,726 --> 01:10:13,766
I can send somebody to get it.

895
01:10:13,853 --> 01:10:15,893
Come, I want to show you something.

896
01:10:22,153 --> 01:10:23,398
All right.

897
01:10:24,823 --> 01:10:25,772
You.

898
01:10:25,990 --> 01:10:26,986
Good memory.

899
01:10:27,200 --> 01:10:29,074
This is Trish, my guardian angel.

900
01:10:29,828 --> 01:10:32,401
- She's helping out with the project.
- What project?

901
01:10:32,497 --> 01:10:36,495
See, a lot of people talk about police
corruption, but no one ever sees it.

902
01:10:37,293 --> 01:10:40,460
I figured I'd be the one to show
it to them, over the Internet.

903
01:10:40,672 --> 01:10:41,917
Have a seat.

904
01:10:43,091 --> 01:10:45,214
- How much?
- How about 25?

905
01:10:45,427 --> 01:10:47,087
With a cut here, a cut there...

906
01:10:47,262 --> 01:10:51,010
it'll double your money easily.
Quickest quarter mil you'll ever make.

907
01:10:51,224 --> 01:10:53,680
I need major weight.
I need it yesterday.

908
01:10:53,893 --> 01:10:56,598
We've been tracking
their activity for months.

909
01:10:56,688 --> 01:10:59,558
I'm compiling the video
on our digital editing system.

910
01:10:59,649 --> 01:11:00,812
You come with me.

911
01:11:00,900 --> 01:11:02,098
Be back in an hour.

912
01:11:02,193 --> 01:11:05,812
When we have enough evidence,
we'll show it to the authorities.

913
01:11:07,991 --> 01:11:10,945
If that doesn't work, we'll
post the video on our website.

914
01:11:11,036 --> 01:11:12,696
Why you pressing me?

915
01:11:12,912 --> 01:11:17,539
Look, if I wanted to bust you,
I'd have brought you in a long time ago.

916
01:11:17,751 --> 01:11:21,700
This is business. I just got a
shitload of product for our next deal.

917
01:11:21,796 --> 01:11:23,374
Incriminating shit.

918
01:11:24,340 --> 01:11:28,041
They think I'm a buyer from the West
Coast looking to score major weight.

919
01:11:28,219 --> 01:11:29,548
They raised it, too.

920
01:11:29,637 --> 01:11:33,386
I don't know how, but they managed
to get $5 million worth of shit.

921
01:11:33,892 --> 01:11:34,887
Piper Tech.

922
01:11:35,393 --> 01:11:36,591
Run number 8.

923
01:11:37,062 --> 01:11:38,805
- You sure?
- Yeah.

924
01:11:40,148 --> 01:11:42,983
Welcome to the inner sanctum,
Mr. Walker.

925
01:11:45,320 --> 01:11:46,779
I always wanted to do that.

926
01:11:46,946 --> 01:11:48,986
You didn't know he was in on it?

927
01:11:49,074 --> 01:11:53,202
"The greatest trick the devil ever pulled
was convince the world he didn't exist."

928
01:11:53,703 --> 01:11:55,411
Where'd you guys get this stuff?

929
01:11:55,497 --> 01:11:58,118
From everywhere. Check it out.

930
01:11:58,792 --> 01:12:01,746
This is our stuff. We have
cameras hidden in everything.

931
01:12:02,337 --> 01:12:05,457
Watches, batteries, purses.
You name it.

932
01:12:07,258 --> 01:12:11,339
This is a little camera that can be
hidden everywhere and can see everything.

933
01:12:11,638 --> 01:12:14,592
And you're the star of a
few of these as well.

934
01:12:16,601 --> 01:12:18,012
Come on, let me go.

935
01:12:18,186 --> 01:12:20,309
Shit, man!

936
01:12:22,190 --> 01:12:23,435
Come on!

937
01:12:23,608 --> 01:12:25,102
Lucky move.

938
01:12:26,361 --> 01:12:27,606
Unlucky face.

939
01:12:28,446 --> 01:12:30,355
T, get us something to drink.

940
01:12:30,615 --> 01:12:34,150
Just because I own a bar don't
mean I'm Isaac from The Love Boat.

941
01:12:34,369 --> 01:12:35,946
A Hennessy Paradis, please.

942
01:12:36,204 --> 01:12:39,371
Yes, master.
Should I get some for Mr. Charlie, too?

943
01:12:42,001 --> 01:12:43,282
What do you think?

944
01:12:43,378 --> 01:12:45,417
I think we need to
take them down now.

945
01:12:45,505 --> 01:12:48,956
Not yet. I want to catch all these
guys at once. Stick it to them.

946
01:12:49,050 --> 01:12:50,710
I won't wait. They
tried to kill me.

947
01:12:50,802 --> 01:12:53,838
I won't let you ruin this.
My brother's ass is on the line.

948
01:12:53,930 --> 01:12:55,508
What's he got to do with it?

949
01:12:55,640 --> 01:12:58,724
Your buddies wanted their own
drug dealer on the street.

950
01:12:58,893 --> 01:13:02,393
Rather than lose him, they framed
Shaun. I got to get him out of jail.

951
01:13:03,231 --> 01:13:05,473
I made my father a
promise before he died.

952
01:13:06,067 --> 01:13:08,226
That I'd always be
my brother's keeper.

953
01:13:09,487 --> 01:13:10,732
I keep my promises.

954
01:13:13,408 --> 01:13:15,650
Where'd you promise
to meet these boys?

955
01:13:16,161 --> 01:13:17,904
Frederick's Cleaners.

956
01:13:19,914 --> 01:13:21,243
After midnight.

957
01:13:21,499 --> 01:13:22,579
I'll need a car.

958
01:13:24,335 --> 01:13:25,616
Give him the keys.

959
01:13:26,713 --> 01:13:28,290
T, the keys.

960
01:13:30,300 --> 01:13:32,707
Come on, man.
My mama don't even drive my car.

961
01:13:32,802 --> 01:13:34,296
Give him the keys.

962
01:13:37,766 --> 01:13:39,308
You scratch it, you buy it.

963
01:14:21,768 --> 01:14:24,010
Nice inconspicuous
car you got there.

964
01:14:24,229 --> 01:14:25,557
Thank you.

965
01:14:25,814 --> 01:14:27,094
What'd you find out?

966
01:14:27,190 --> 01:14:28,981
Piper Tech was hit by cops.

967
01:14:29,401 --> 01:14:30,646
- Cops?
- Yeah.

968
01:14:31,319 --> 01:14:32,315
Come on, Boyd.

969
01:14:32,570 --> 01:14:35,904
Strutt, Useldinger, Montini,
they're all dirty.

970
01:14:37,951 --> 01:14:41,071
Are you positive?
What proof do you have?

971
01:14:41,162 --> 01:14:42,158
Start the car.

972
01:14:57,220 --> 01:14:58,798
Get the car! Let's go!

973
01:15:00,932 --> 01:15:02,592
- Is that proof enough?
- Yeah.

974
01:15:02,809 --> 01:15:03,840
Now move.

975
01:15:13,945 --> 01:15:15,902
Step on it. We got him.

976
01:15:50,315 --> 01:15:51,346
Come on!

977
01:15:55,028 --> 01:15:57,151
- There he is.
- Pop him now!

978
01:15:58,073 --> 01:15:59,152
Shit!

979
01:16:02,911 --> 01:16:03,907
Hold on!

980
01:16:16,216 --> 01:16:18,789
- I always said women are bad drivers.
- I agree.

981
01:16:24,516 --> 01:16:26,259
- There he is!
- Yeah.

982
01:16:29,270 --> 01:16:31,263
Get up on them!

983
01:16:37,028 --> 01:16:38,143
Shit!

984
01:16:39,197 --> 01:16:41,106
Shit! Goddamn!

985
01:16:44,452 --> 01:16:46,528
Get out of the way!

986
01:16:56,715 --> 01:16:58,541
Get out of the way!

987
01:16:58,800 --> 01:17:01,338
- Go right.
- Going left.

988
01:17:02,887 --> 01:17:04,050
Get up to him!

989
01:17:04,431 --> 01:17:05,889
Shoot him!

990
01:17:26,870 --> 01:17:27,901
